Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: keep beacon completions out of TX hang tracking

The TX hang watchdog checks the four data queues, but every completion with
a TXWI clears its counter. In AP mode, regularly completed beacons keep
the counter below its threshold even when the data queues stop making
progress.

Use the queue ID stored in the TXWI cache to clear the counter only for
data queue completions. This restores the original scope of completion
progress tracking. Progress on one data queue can still mask a stalled
different data queue. Independent per-queue tracking is outside this
change.

Fixes: fe5b5ab52e9d ("mt76: unify queue tx cleanup code")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
--- a/mt7603/mac.c
+++ b/mt7603/mac.c
@@ -1333,7 +1333,8 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	dev->tx_hang_check = 0;
+	if (e->txwi->qid <= MT_TXQ_BK)
+		dev->tx_hang_check = 0;
 	mt76_tx_complete_skb(mdev, e->wcid, skb);
 }
 
